<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Majapahit Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Majapahit</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Majapahit Empire was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-buddhist">Hindu-Buddhist</a> maritime state based in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, founded in 1293 after the repulse of a Mongol expedition. Under the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gajah-mada">Gajah Mada</a> and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayam-wuruk">Hayam Wuruk</a> in the fourteenth century, it claimed authority across much of the Indonesian archipelago. It succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> as the leading power of the region before declining in the fifteenth and early sixteenth centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire.jpg" alt="Majapahit Empire" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: source: BP47Dhorifah, svg: Puck04 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naval_flag_of_Majapahit_Kingdom.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
